From: Brian 'redbeard' Harrington <redbeard@dead-city.org>
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Platform/Spacemit/K3: Cpu.asl _LPI first cut + \_SB platform _OSC (Task 9)

Platform/Spacemit/K3: Cpu.asl _LPI first cut + \_SB platform _OSC (Task 9)

Add _LPI to every ACPI0007 processor device: two non-retentive
platform states per the FFH spec and the HSM suspend audit
(task9-hsm-suspend-audit-2026-11-20.md):

- CPU_NR: FFH address (1<<60)|0x90000000 = 0x1000000090000000,
  min-residency 950us, wake 500us
- CLUSTER_NR: FFH address (1<<60)|0x91000000 = 0x1000000091000000,
  min-residency 2700us, wake 1100us

Every state package carries Flags bit 0 (ENABLED): flatten_lpi_states
skips states without ACPI_LPI_STATE_FLAGS_ENABLED, so Flags=0 would
flatten to zero states and the backend count>1 check would fail with
-ENODEV.

The RISC-V FFH encoding is (1ULL<<60)|sbi_suspend_param with
bits[59:32] reserved zero - the param lives in the LOW 32 bits (the
CPPC FFH convention already in this file). Both states use the proven
PMU vote + WFI + in-place-resume mechanism from k3_corepm.c; the
kernel's RISC-V LPI backend requires >1 flattened state, so both are
exposed. Package layout per ACPI 6.5 _LPI: {MinResidency,
WakeLatency, Count, StatePkgs...} (iASL-validated; states are
10-element packages with the FFH Register at index 6). Latencies are
vendor DT values - measure before freezing. NOTE: the kernel's LPI
naming starts at index 0 with the FIRST flattened state (no inserted
safe/WFI state on this path): expect LPI-0=CPU_NR, LPI-1=CLUSTER_NR.

Add the \\_SB platform-wide _OSC (UUID 0811B06E-...) confirming
PCLPI (0x80) ONLY: acpi_processor_get_lpi_info() gates _LPI parsing
on osc_pc_lpi_support_confirmed, set exclusively by this handshake.
The buffer is 2 DWORDs (u32 capbuf[2]: Query/Status, Support - NO
Control DWORD; a CDW3 at offset 8 would raise AE_AML_BUFFER_LIMIT).
The method handles both handshake passes. PR3/S3, GED, hotplug-OST
not confirmed; unknown UUIDs fail. (PCI0's _OSC keeps CDW3:
pci_root.c passes capbuf[5].)

Validation: full RELEASE build; built DSDT decompiles 8x _LPI with
Flags=One, correct FFH addresses, and the \\_SB _OSC. Hardware gates
closed so far (live evidence): _OSC presence (OS control mask
[00000080]), buffer contract, FFH encoding rejection. Next cycle is
the first with all four gates (presence, buffer, encoding, flags)
correct.
---
